# Backend image (Dockerfile): only what Django runs gets in. Everything else stays out, so the
# build never copies local clutter (Claude worktrees, node_modules, backups, editor folders)
# and every rebuild copies a few MB instead of the whole folder. The web image has its own list
# (web/Dockerfile.dockerignore).
*
!apps
!config
!manage.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
